    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14447" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-taedet</span></b> , ‡ tisum (acc. to Paul. ex
			<i><span class="en">Fest.
			p. 72, 18</span></i>), 2, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. impers.</i>, <i>to be very tired
			of</i>, <i>disgusted with</i>, <i>to
				loathe</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haud quod tui me neque domi distaedeat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Am. 1, 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">me cum hoc ipso distaedet loqui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter. Ph. 5, 8, 22</span></i>
			.</div>
